## Context

The primary checkout's `.env` (gitignored, mtime 2026-05-24) holds nine
inline values, six of them live credentials: `AGENT_GH_TOKEN`,
`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `HF_TOKEN`, `ZENODO_TOKEN`, `HAL_PASSWORD`,
`OPENAI_API_KEY` (plus `HAL_ID`, `AGENT_GIT_NAME`, `AGENT_GIT_EMAIL`).
Audit of 2026-09-24, value-equality booleans only, no value printed:

- Every inline value equals a `~/.config/keys/` entry: `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
  equals `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_AEDIST` in `openrouter.env`; the other eight equal
  their same-name entry. Deleting them loses no value. (Equality says nothing
  about liveness; the smoke criterion below covers that.)
- **Ambient residency.** The harness `bash-env.sh` strict-parses every project
  `.env` and exports each unprotected name into every bash subprocess, so these
  credentials sit in the environment of every shell opened in this repo —
  what harness tracker 0942 set out to end. Harness 0955 proposes a
  loader-side refusal.
- **Group-readable.** The file was mode 0664, group `untrusted-runner` (the
  sandbox user's primary group). Tightened to 0600 on 2026-09-24; all nine
  values were readable to that account before.
- **0679 landed, then was undone.** 0679's Outcome section records the `.env`
  reduced on 2026-07-14 to a single `KEYS=` selection line, with the
  pre-migration snapshot kept as `.env.bak-premigration`. Today the `.env`
  carries the inline values again, its mtime (2026-05-24) predates that
  migration, and `.env.bak-premigration` no longer exists. That is consistent
  with the snapshot having been moved back over `.env` — plausibly after
  harness 0945 removed `KEYS=` support on 2026-09-17 and the variables stopped
  loading. Cause not established: no surviving session log mentions the
  snapshot. The `AGENT_GH_TOKEN` 0679 found dead now equals the central value,
  so the restored copy is not simply that snapshot, or the central token
  changed since; either way, do not trust 0679's verdict table.
- **Consumers.** `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is still read by `src/aedist/harness.py`
  (333, 339), `src/aedist/pdf2md_openrouter_doc.py:54` and
  `scripts/audit_argument.py:82`. The adapters read `OPENAI_API_KEY_AEDIST`,
  `QWEN_API_KEY_AEDIST`, `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,
  `TAVILY_API_KEY`, none of which is in `.env`: those runs need an explicit
  export today. `experiments/acquire.mk:180-187,215` greps `ZOTERO_API_KEY`
  out of `../.env` (falling back to `~/.claude/.env`) into an exported Make
  variable — against the file's own ENV POLICY — and `build_corpus.py:397`
  reads it; the `preflight` target requires the line in `../.env`.
- History is clean: `.env` never committed; no match in `git log --all -p` for
  `sk-or-v1-`, `sk-proj-`, `ghp_`, `github_pat_`, `hf_` token shapes.

## Approach

The repo policy (ticket 0240, `tests/test_secret_loading_policy.py`,
`experiments/common.mk` ENV POLICY) says source code reads keys only from its
environment and never opens key files; Make injects them via
`UV_RUN := uv run --project .. --env-file ../.env`. That contract can stay,
with the injection source moved from the project `.env` to the keystore, per
invocation, so no shell carries the keys.

Decide at implementation, and record in the commit:

- **Granularity.** One global `UV_RUN` with several `--env-file` gives every
  target every listed provider, and a keystore file can hold other projects'
  keys (`openrouter.env` holds active keys for four projects). Least privilege needs
  per-target selection: either per-provider `UV_RUN_<provider>` variables, or
  a small Make-level helper that extracts only the named variables (and can
  rename, e.g. `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_AEDIST` → `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`) into the
  child's environment. First check that the installed `uv` accepts repeated
  `--env-file` and which one wins on a conflict.
- **Names.** Either rename the readers listed above to the keystore names, or
  map at injection. Whichever is chosen, every reader moves together.
- **Reproducibility.** The 2026-04-30 rationale ("a fresh clone with `.env`
  populated runs end-to-end") loses its only documented setup path; document
  the keystore file names a collaborator or CI must provide instead.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `.env` holds no credential value, checked mechanically: no line of it
      names a variable defined in any `~/.config/keys/*.env` (names-only)
- [ ] With `BASH_ENV` pointing at the live harness loader and the environment
      otherwise cleared (`env -i HOME=$HOME BASH_ENV=… bash -c env`, run in the
      repo root), none of the credential names above appears
- [ ] `UV_RUN` and every docstring or message that says `--env-file ../.env`
      now resolve from the keystore; the ENV POLICY header in
      `experiments/acquire.mk` and `common.mk` rewritten
- [ ] `ZOTERO_API_KEY` in `acquire.mk` (180-187, 215, 231-234) migrated to the
      same mechanism; `preflight` no longer requires a `.env` line
- [ ] The `_NEEDS_ENV` sentinel (`acquire.mk:65-70`) still passes for the
      targets it guards, or is replaced by a keystore-presence check
- [ ] Each provider's key reaches its consumer: one minimal authenticated call
      per provider (listing models or equivalent, no generation), and the
      author approves any call that costs money before it runs
- [ ] `tests/test_secret_loading_policy.py` updated to the new contract and
      still guarding against `load_dotenv` / hard-coded key paths in `src/`
- [ ] Rotation decided for each of the six credentials that were readable to
      `untrusted-runner`: rotate, or accept the risk with a reason; recorded here
- [ ] Log note here correcting 0679's closing claim (not reopened)
- [ ] `make check` passes
